WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.289 --> 00:00:01.809
Welcome to sprint 3,

1
00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.210
testing and iteration day of our TSA Dragster build.

2
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:06.849
Before we finalize everything,

3
00:00:06.929 --> 00:00:10.159
we need to run test number 1 on the incline test ramp.

4
00:00:10.489 --> 00:00:11.489
For a competitive car,

5
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.329
our target benchmark is rolling smoothly as far as

6
00:00:14.329 --> 00:00:17.510
possible while tracking completely straight down the track.

7
00:00:17.969 --> 00:00:20.059
Let's release the car and record our baseline data.

8
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.559
For our first test and iteration loop,

9
00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.829
we run the test and record the exact data metric.

10
00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:29.930
As the dragster rolls down the ramp,

11
00:00:30.159 --> 00:00:34.310
you notice it pulling hard to the right and losing momentum halfway down the track.

12
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.470
It only travels for 10 ft when measured on the track.

13
00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.069
That is far shorter than the expected outcome.

14
00:00:40.369 --> 00:00:42.970
The diagonal travel is clearly causing issues.

15
00:00:44.759 --> 00:00:46.029
Instead of guessing,

16
00:00:46.319 --> 00:00:49.540
step 2 of the loop is diagnosing the root cause.

17
00:00:50.119 --> 00:00:54.189
Flipping the car over for a visual inspection reveals two connected flaws.

18
00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:54.720
First,

19
00:00:54.799 --> 00:00:57.200
you see the rear wheels are installed off center

20
00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.220
and are making contact with the car body.

21
00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.119
Second,

22
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.519
there are not washers or wheel clips holding the wheels in the proper alignment.

23
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.959
Now it is time for step 3,

24
00:01:09.239 --> 00:01:11.440
justifying a specific modification

25
00:01:11.599 --> 00:01:13.019
in your iteration log.

26
00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.050
Scroll down to the form right below this video and write a data-driven entry.

27
00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:18.879
First,

28
00:01:19.129 --> 00:01:21.169
state the exact recorded metrics,

29
00:01:21.559 --> 00:01:25.339
then explain what you identified as the root cause for the problem.

30
00:01:25.879 --> 00:01:26.400
Finally,

31
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.199
specify the exact changes you will make for iteration number 2,

32
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.459
such as adjusting the wheels or

33
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.879
adding additional hardware to correct the problem.